# Club & Grub - World 9, stage 2 in co-op: "The Roc's Spire" (designer D9a). The co-op file of levels/w9_l2.lvl
# (DESIGN.md A.6 / D.10, LEVEL_DESIGN.md 15.7): the same spire with P2's start and two co-op gates, each with its
# tablet and a checkpoint behind:
#  - 'brace' (C, A.6's Brace corridor; the lee is no gate, G55): the lower terrace becomes a sunken hall exactly
#    4 rows high and 17 cells long; its Bull Rex sleeps at the far end until the pair has stepped in, then charges,
#    and only a Brace Wall of two crouching heroes stops it (dazed 44 ticks, head open); it keeps the hall's door;
#  - 'drive': the final gap is 13 cells of tar without its drop clouds (9 fell to a lone hero's gust jump, G79): a
#    charged Batter Up line drive puts one hero across; he steps on the latch plate there and the cloud slab over
#    the gap sinks into a bridge for his partner.
#    The slate stack over the cloud hall is 14 rows high here (5 more than in the solo file; DESIGN G67): from its
#    top a lone hero stepped onto the raised slab, and he reached that top from the painting's cloud - 6 rows under
#    it - by a hop jump, or by a pogo jump on the painting's spot (130 px). Now it stands 11 rows over that cloud.
# The Guards of the solo file are left out (a Guard in co-op needs a 4-row hall, LEVEL_DESIGN 15.7.5): tribesmen
# keep their places. Traits: the heavy Bull Rex, lone tribesmen and storm pterodactyls (over a third of the
# records); the valley Rollers stay plain - a bond on the two slopes would lie on one throw line (G36).

